---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Projects">
  <div class="page-wrapper">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:6px;">Projects & Builds</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:36px;">Things I have built in my free time. Source on GitHub.</p>
      <div class="project-grid">

        <div class="project-card">
          <div class="project-icon">AI</div>
          <h3>Gemma 4 Local Starter</h3>
          <p>Run Google's Gemma 4 locally on your machine using Ollama and Python. Three escalating demos: basic chat, document summarization, and personal notes Q&A. Zero API cost. Zero data leaving your machine.</p>
          <div class="project-stack">
            <span class="stack-badge">Python</span>
            <span class="stack-badge">Ollama</span>
            <span class="stack-badge">Gemma 4</span>
            <span class="stack-badge">Windows</span>
          </div>
          <div style="margin-top:1rem;display:flex;gap:12px;">
            <a href="https://github.com/Bornism/gemma4-local-starter" target="_blank" style="color:var(--accent);font-size:.9rem;">GitHub Repo</a>
            <a href="/blog/2026-06-08-gemma4-local-starter" style="color:var(--accent);font-size:.9rem;">Read the Post</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card" style="border-style:dashed;">
          <div class="project-icon">WIP</div>
          <h3>More coming soon</h3>
          <p>Always building. Next up: a proper RAG pipeline with vector embeddings and an AI agent build using MCP on Google Cloud.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
